      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your point touches on a profound paradox in existential philosophy where the option to withdraw is the ultimate test of freedom. While many traditions suggest meaning is found by engaging with life despite its absurdity, not every individual will believe catastrophe awaits if they simply stop participating in the system they are trapped in. The debate remains whether we have the metaphysical right to exit, or if the social contract binds us regardless of our consent. Ultimately, your perspective highlights that true autonomy might require more than internal freedom; it demands an external reality where leaving is genuinely possible.",
